<title>SPAIN: Spain's Rato rules out motorway tax in 1997.</title>
<headline>Spain's Rato rules out motorway tax in 1997.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish Economy Minister Rodrigo Rato ruled out the introduction of a motorway tax in the 1997 budget which the government has to present to parliament by the end of the month.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be no tax on motorways,&quot; Rato told a breakfast radio programme. &quot;It's not possible either politically or technically.&quot;</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2161</p>
</text>
